# The z-ai-web-dev-sdk does NOT read from environment variables.
# It reads a JSON config file from one of these locations (in order):
#   ./.z-ai-config           (project root — recommended)
#   ~/.z-ai-config            (user home)
#   /etc/.z-ai-config         (system-wide)
#
# Create ./.z-ai-config with the following shape:
#
#   {
#     "baseUrl": "https://api.z.ai/v1",
#     "apiKey": "YOUR_API_KEY",
#     "chatId": "OPTIONAL",
#     "userId": "OPTIONAL"
#   }
#
# .z-ai-config is in .gitignore and will never be committed.
#
# For Vercel / Netlify / other serverless hosts that don't have a
# filesystem you can write to at build time, the SDK can also be
# initialised in code — see the SDK README for the env-var pattern:
#   https://www.npmjs.com/package/z-ai-web-dev-sdk
